
IF YOU'VE CLONED REPOSITORY ONTO A NEW DEVICE:
0. remove venv folder
1. create a venv ("python -m venv venv")
2. activate venv ("source venv/bin/activate")
3. try "python sockServer.py"
      -> it will give an error about a missing library
      -> pip install that library
4. repeat step 3 until running sockServer prints: "Server running..."
5. ctrl+C


CONNECTING TO RASPBERRY:
1. connect the raspberry and your device to the same network 
2. make sure raspberry's code has your device's ip address:
     -> find your device's ip with "hostname -I"
     -> go to raspberry's python file Robotti/Code/Server/sockClient.py
     -> change the ip address on line 5 to your ip address
3. run sockServer.py on your device
     -> activate venv ("source venv/bin/activate")
     -> "python sockServer.py"
     -> when the code prints "Server running..." proceed to the next step
4. run runMartti.py from raspberry ("sudo python Code/Server/runMartti.py")
     -> in a while it should say a connection has been made on your device:
       Connection from ('172.20.10.11', 39964) has been established.
       starting stt...
       Loading Whisper model...
       Always listening...
       with inputstream
5. speak into the mic
      -> ai will soon transcribe your speech and print what it has transcribed. This command is sent to raspberry. 
        Speech detected
        Transcribing...
        your command
6. when finished, give command "turn off" and the raspberry pi code will end.
7. to end the code on your device just ctrl+c many times 
8. exit the venv with "deactivate"


IF MICROPHONE DOES NOT SEEM TO WORK: (it does not say speech detected)
1. connect microphone while device is turned off
2. check from settings that input device is set to wireless mic DIGITAL input
IF RUNNING STILL DOES NOT WORK
1. activate venv ("source venv/bin/activate")
2. "python actualrealtime_stt2queue.py"
3. try speaking into mic. if it transcribes, yippee!!
4. ctrl+C
5. run sockServer.py again.
IF IT SSTTIILL does NOT work...
   -> you're on your own ;D




DEFAULT COMMANDS YOU CAN USE:
"stop" -> stops anything the robot is currently doing
"play" -> plays 440Hz
"play no surprises" -> plays "no surprises" by Radiohead
"go forwards"
"go backwards"
"turn left"
"turn right"
"I love you"
"flash" -> cool light effect
"avoid" -> avoid obstacles mode 
"happy" -> makes robot happy
"sad" -> makes robot sad
"execute order 66" -> muahahahaa

"off" -> disconnects raspberry from your device.


